\n" [:option {:value "351326"} "Featherweight (≤68 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "351352"} "Welterweight (≤80 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "351378"} "Heavyweight (&gt;80 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "351404"} "Flyweight (≤49 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "351430"} "Featherweight (≤57 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "351456"} "Welterweight (≤67 kilograms), Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "900799"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "901187"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "28198"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "28430"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "262293"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "325182"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "19004482"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007730"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/619"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Heavyweight (&gt;67 kilograms), Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "20 – 21 August 2016"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/903"} "Arena Carioca 3, Parque Olímpico da Barra, Barra da Tijuca, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/351482"} "16 from 16 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament. All fighters losing to the finalists in each pool advance to repêchage tournament for the bronze medal."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The women’s heavyweight division contained the most diverse selection of fighters in Rio, and picking a winner in advance was no easy task. The 2008 champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/117404"} "María Espinoza"] " of Mexico could only win bronze at London in 2012m=, but was the top seed in Rio and had a good chance of regaining her title. Standing in her way was the tall number two seed, China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/129691"} "Zheng Shuyin"] ", who came into the Games with a good recent run of success behind her. She won a silver medal at the 2015 World Championships and won the 2015 Grand Prix Series final. She also possessed a good varied collection of kicks in her armoury. Britain’s number three seed " [:a {:href "/athletes/130287"} "Bianca “Queen Bee” Walkden"] " was hit with injury in 2014 but bounced back to win the 2015 World Championship, but she had lost three times to Zheng. Walkden’s boyfriend was the British-born welterweight " [:a {:href "/athletes/117437"} "Aaron Cook"] ", who represented Moldova in Rio. The 2012 gold medallist " [:a {:href "/athletes/122193"} "Milica Mandić"] " of Serbia, who won a silver medal at the 2016 European Championships, was one of the most popular people in taekwondo and was seeded at number six."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Walkden had the biggest win of the opening round, winning 14-1 against " [:a {:href "/athletes/131360"} "Samantha Kassman"] " of Papua New Guinea. The top two seeds also progressed to the quarter-final and top seed Espinoza came through to the last four after a sudden-death win, and her semi-final against " [:a {:href "/athletes/132169"} "Jackie Galloway"] " of the USA was even closer. After four rounds it was 0-0 and the top seed won though on the superiority ruling."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the other half of the draw Zheng and Walkden met in the semi-final meaning the top four seeds contested the two semis. After a very close contest that went to sudden-death, Zheng  won it with a head kick. Walkden had some consolation by taking the bronze medal while Galloway won the other bronze medal match. Zheng controlled the final against the two-time Olympic medallist Maria Espinoza and ran out the 5-1 winner. Espinoza’s silver added to her gold in Beijing and bronze in London for a full set of medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/129691"} "Zheng Shuyin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117404"} "María Espinoza"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/MEX"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/MEX.png"}] "MEX"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/130287"} "Bianca Walkden"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/132169"} "Jackie Galloway"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/123575"} "Wiam Dislam"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/MAR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/MAR.png"}] "MAR"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [: